# Results produced by tools/benchmarks/pqc (`make run` writes here).
#
# Local runs are the contributor's own business and are NOT committed by
# default: everything is ignored unless it is explicitly listed below.
# Publishing a run is therefore a deliberate two-line act — un-ignore it here,
# and add it to tools/benchmarks/pqc/analyze/published_runs.txt, which is the
# manifest `make merge` reads. Ad-hoc runs sitting in this directory can never
# leak into the published dashboard dataset by accident.
#
# Full provenance for every file below: ../README.md and published_runs.txt.

*.json

# Tiny macOS smoke output shipped as a schema example, not measurement data.
!example-*.json

# ---- current published set (schema 2.0.0) ----------------------------------
# Baseline-grade RPi5 reference run (narrowed-sudo runner).
!rasberrypi5-20260730T212145Z.json
# Reference-platform verification run of THIS tree (28-check gate):
# reference-grade, zero warnings, medians within ±0.4% of the published
# 20260730 baseline — third consecutive reproduction. Not yet swapped into
# published_runs.txt (that rebuild of merged.json is a follow-up decision).
!rasberrypi5-20260811T211615Z.json
# Cross-platform runs: Apple M3, Apple M4 Pro, Fedora 44 x86_64.
!mehmetmac-20260719T224937Z.json
!Mac-20260730T134951Z.json
!fedora-20260730T120637Z.json

# ---- role-asymmetry stress runs (schema stress-1.0.0) ----------------------
# Different measurement, different grade: these carry is_stress_grade and never
# is_baseline_grade, and analyze/published_runs.txt does not list them (they are
# not dashboard inputs). See ../sender-receiver-asymmetry.md.
#
# Three runs on a quiet machine (1-min load 1.66 / 1.99 / 1.64). The report
# quotes their MEDIAN and states the spread; one run cannot tell a real
# difference from the scheduler having a bad second.
# Reference-platform sweep: RPi5, governor=performance, load 0.00 at start,
# X25519 control 1.0004 — the file the report's reference-platform paragraph
# rests on.
!stress-rasberrypi5-20260812T043436Z.json
# Apple M3 median-of-three (1-min loads 3.78/8.05/5.86 — an interactive
# machine; ratios still within a few percent of the quiet-M4 medians, which is
# the load-robustness claim exercised on a third platform).
!stress-mehmetmac-20260812T111720Z.json
!stress-mehmetmac-20260812T112638Z.json
!stress-mehmetmac-20260812T113607Z.json
!stress-Mac-20260807T163719Z.json
!stress-Mac-20260807T165015Z.json
!stress-Mac-20260807T171426Z.json
# Kept deliberately: a sweep that started at 1-min load 113. It is the evidence
# for the report's claim that competing load distorts absolute latency
# (+26-33%) while leaving the ratios within 4%; deleting it would leave that
# claim unsupported. NOT part of the medians.
!stress-Mac-20260807T155820Z.json

